; Portal ROM (main code) block definitions for z80dasm
; Main code is loaded at F800h after bootstrapper copies it from ROM.
;
; NOTE: Address F802 contains the 8085 SIM opcode (0x30).
; z80dasm would decode it as "jr nc,..." (Z80 relative jump), eating
; the next byte and desyncing the disassembly. We mark it as a single
; byte of data. In the annotated disassembly, add a comment:
;   defb 030h   ; SIM — set interrupt mask (8085-only)
;
sim_opcode: start 0xF802 last 0xF802 type bytedata
; Data: floppy parameter string "S0(" + bytes
str_floppy_params: start 0xFAFD last 0xFB03 type bytedata
; Data: prompt string "\t PORTAL..\0"
str_portal: start 0xFB8C last 0xFB96 type bytedata
